[E] BOUND ON THIS REPORT'S T-43 EVIDENCE. The T-43 line in this file was: "bun test packages/mpd-workmate-plugin -> 28 pass / 0 fail (a normal session is never refused)". That reading is a NORMAL-SESSION case only (the guard returns early when DSH_HOME is unset) and it does NOT exercise the isolated-boot path the guard exists for. It is true and it is narrow; it is not a certificate for "the T-43 guard works", and it must not be cited as one.
[F] MECHANISM OF THE DEFECT the QA lane found (measured read-only, 4 arms, my own probes; NO file was edited — the fix is t62's task):
    ARM 1  node, HOME=<sandbox> + DSH_HOME=<sandbox> AT PROCESS START (the real QA-boot shape)          -> REFUSED 403 real-home-refused
    ARM 2a bun, real HOME=/root at start, HOME+DSH_HOME set AT RUNTIME to <sandbox> (t23's case shape)  -> ALLOWED
    ARM 2b node, DSH_HOME unset at start (normal session)                                              -> ALLOWED
    ARM 2c node, sandbox HOME at start + MPD_DSH_WORKMATE_ALLOW_REAL_HOME=1                            -> ALLOWED
    (control) node, DSH_HOME set + HOME repointed at RUNTIME                                           -> REFUSED — because plain Node's os.homedir() follows the LIVE env
    THE DISCRIMINATOR: the guard's allow-branch requires resolve(HOME) !== resolve(homedir()). Under bun (the plugin's runtime) os.homedir() is frozen at process start (the code comment relies on exactly that), so the branch is reachable ONLY when HOME is changed AFTER start. A real QA boot puts HOME=<sandbox> in the process-start env, where both values are equal -> refused. t23's four in-process cases passed because guard-cases.mjs assigns process.env.HOME in-process under bun: a shape no verifier's boot can reproduce.
    CONSEQUENCE: the guard refuses the very sandbox its own documentation prescribes; it is inverted, not merely noisy, under a real mounted boot. Fix belongs to t62; re-verification belongs to t21. This file's lane-F verdict stands as a bound, not as a certificate.
    REPRODUCE: `DSH_HOME=/tmp/h HOME=/tmp/h node --input-type=module -e 'import("/root/dshProj/my-power-dsh/packages/mpd-workmate-plugin/dist/index.js").then(m=>{try{m.assertMutationSandboxed("x");console.log("ALLOWED")}catch(e){console.log("REFUSED",e.code)}})'` -> REFUSED.

